<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lý Chiêu Hoàng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1218–1278</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Ly Chieu Hoang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lý Chiêu Hoàng was the only reigning empress in Vietnamese history and the last ruler of the Lý dynasty, enthroned as a child in 1224. In 1225 the regent Trần Thủ Độ arranged her marriage to his young nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-thai-tong">Trần Cảnh</a> and her abdication in his favour. Trần Cảnh became emperor Trần Thái Tông, founding the Trần dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ly-chieu-hoang.jpg" alt="Lý Chiêu Hoàng" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sử dụng hợp lí · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_L%C3%BD_Chi%C3%AAu_Ho%C3%A0ng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
